[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The SBCERS 2020 RFP states in the Minimum Qualifications section that the proposing firm must have been in business for at least five years. This requirement applies to firms providing services similar to those in the Scope of Services.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>Five-year minimum.</NAME>
<CONTENT>In the SBCERS 2020 Request for Proposals for Discretionary Private Equity Consultant Services, the proposing firm must have been in business at least five (5) years.

Relevant language from Section I.F, “Minimum Qualifications for Proposal”:
- “The firm must have been in business at least five (5) years providing services similar to those described in the Scope of Services section.”

A related qualification in the same section also states:
- “The organization must have been providing investment management services for Private Equity investment transactions for five or more years...”

So, the direct answer to your question is: at least five (5) years.</CONTENT>
