[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The Arizona PSPRS RFP for non-discretionary investment consultant services evaluates proposals using four weighted criteria. The criteria focus on relevant experience and staffing, service capabilities, ability to meet service requirements, and overall cost.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>PSPRS RFP scoring weights.</NAME>
<CONTENT>Arizona PSPRS states that proposals for non-discretionary investment consultant services will be evaluated based on written submissions and, if applicable, finalist interviews. Interviews are not guaranteed, so written proposals must contain all information the proposer wants considered.

The evaluation criteria and weights are:

1. Relevant knowledge and experience — 25%
   - Relevant knowledge and experience in similar consulting engagements
   - Current organizational capacity to provide experienced staff
   - Ability to perform the services described in the Scope of Services

2. Quality and extent of firm capabilities — 30%
   This is the highest-weighted category and covers the firm’s capabilities in:
   - Strategic advice
   - New investment identification and evaluation
   - Operational due diligence
   - Investment due diligence
   - Manager performance reporting and monitoring
   - Back office support

3. Demonstrated ability to meet service requirements — 25%
   - Ability to communicate with the CIO and investment team
   - Ability to communicate with Trustees and the Board’s consultant
   - Responsiveness to ongoing and special issues
   - Operational plan for fulfilling duties
   - Quality of professional staff assigned to the contract

4. Overall cost of proposed services — 20%
   - Overall cost of the firm’s proposed services

In short, PSPRS uses a 100% weighted evaluation model:
- 25% experience and staffing
- 30% capabilities
- 25% service delivery and responsiveness
- 20% cost

The RFP also notes that the contract will be awarded to the proposal deemed to provide the best value to the System, with consideration given to competence, knowledge, reputation, experience, qualifications, methodology, responsiveness, and cost.</CONTENT>
[role=assistant] <SUMMARY>
# Markdown Briefing: Arizona PSPRS RFP Evaluation Criteria and Weights

## Overview
The **Arizona Public Safety Personnel Retirement System (PSPRS)** evaluates proposals for **non-discretionary investment consultant services** using a **100% weighted scoring model** based primarily on the written proposal, with finalist interviews used only **if applicable**.

> **Important:** Because interviews are **not guaranteed**, proposers must include all relevant information in their written submissions.

## Evaluation Criteria and Weights

### 1. **Relevant Knowledge and Experience — 25%**
Assesses:
- Experience in similar consulting engagements
- Organizational capacity to provide experienced staff
- Ability to perform the services described in the Scope of Services

### 2. **Quality and Extent of Firm Capabilities — 30%**
**Highest-weighted category.** Assesses capabilities in:
- Strategic advice
- New investment identification and evaluation
- Operational due diligence
- Investment due diligence
- Manager performance reporting and monitoring
- Back office support

### 3. **Demonstrated Ability to Meet Service Requirements — 25%**
Assesses:
- Communication with the CIO and investment team
- Communication with Trustees and the Board’s consultant
- Responsiveness to ongoing and special issues
- Operational plan for fulfilling duties
- Quality of professional staff assigned to the contract

### 4. **Overall Cost of Proposed Services — 20%**
Assesses:
- Total proposed cost of services

## Weighting Summary
- **25%** — Experience and staffing
- **30%** — Firm capabilities
- **25%** — Service delivery and responsiveness
- **20%** — Cost

## Best-Value Standard
PSPRS indicates that award will be made to the proposal offering the **best value** to the System, considering:
- Competence
- Knowledge
- Reputation
- Experience
- Qualifications
- Methodology
- Responsiveness
- Cost
</SUMMARY>
