[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The Monroe County 457(b) RFP expressly cites the New York State Deferred Compensation Board Model Plan provisions that answer both parts of the question. It states the minimum annual deferral amount and the deadline for investing participant deferrals after receipt.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>Model Plan minimums.</NAME>
<CONTENT>The RFP’s “Specifications of the Model Plan” provides the relevant requirements:

- Under **Section 3.2(a)**, the **minimum deferral amount is $260 for any plan year**.
- Under **Section 4.1**, participant deferrals must be invested **no later than two (2) business days following receipt thereof**, in accordance with the participant’s investment directions.

So, the answer is: **$260 minimum deferral per plan year**, and deferrals must be invested within **2 business days after receipt**.</CONTENT>
