# Markdown Briefing: 457 / Deferred Compensation RFP Contract Terms

## Summary
The deferred compensation / 457 plan recordkeeping RFPs in the corpus propose **three main term structures**:

- **Up to 5 years**
- **A negotiable term**, with pricing requested for **5-, 7-, and 10-year structures**
- **A 3-year initial term** with **up to 7 one-year extensions**

## RFP-by-RFP Term Structure

### **Monroe County Deferred Compensation Plan (2023)**
- **Initial term:** **Up to 5 years**
- **Renewal/extension options:** **None separately stated**
- **Other term-related provisions:**
  - Subject to **periodic Committee review**
  - Committee may **cancel at the end of any contract year** with **30 days’ advance written notice**
  - On expiration or termination, replacement contracts would be awarded through applicable procedures

### **City of Temple City, California – 457 Deferred Compensation Plan (2020)**
- **Initial term:** **Not fixed; to be negotiated** at the end of the RFP process
- **Renewal/extension options:**
  - Pricing requested for:
    - **5 years**
    - **7 years**
    - **10 years**
  - The **7- and 10-year structures** assume the City would **extend the contract later**
- **Key limitation:**
  - The RFP notes that **purchasing rules may cap the available term at 5 years**
- **Takeaway:** The term is **negotiable**, but longer durations beyond 5 years are **contingent on future extensions** and may not ultimately be available

### **Clark County RFP #955 – Deferred Compensation 457 Plan Administrator**
- **Initial term:** **3 years**
  - **January 1, 2027 – December 31, 2029**
- **Renewal/extension options:** **Up to 7 additional one-year extensions**
- **Extension structure:**
  - Extensions are on the **same terms and conditions, except cost**
  - **Option-year pricing** is reviewed before each extension
- **Other term-related provisions:**
  - County may terminate with **30 days’ written notice** for unsatisfactory performance

## Overall Takeaways
- **Monroe County:** **Up to 5 years**, with **no separate extension ladder**
- **Temple City:** **Negotiated term**, with pricing requested for **5/7/10 years**; longer terms depend on **future extensions** and may be constrained by a **5-year purchasing limit**
- **Clark County:** **3-year base term** plus **up to 7 one-year extensions**

## Scope Note
Excluded from this summary are RFPs that were **not 457/deferred compensation recordkeeping procurements** or did **not provide usable term information**.
</SUMMARY>
