[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The evidence directly answers all four parts of the question from the 2021 PRI covering note. It states when the first questionnaire was launched, who adopted it, when the update working group was established, and how long LPs and GPs had been providing comments.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>Key dates and adoption.</NAME>
<CONTENT>- The first version of the PRI Limited Partners Private Equity Responsible Investment Due Diligence Questionnaire (DDQ) was launched in <b>2015</b>.
- It was adopted by <b>ILPA (Institutional Limited Partners Association)</b> as part of the broader <b>ILPA DDQ</b>.
- The working group for the 2021 update was established in <b>early 2021</b>.
- LPs and GPs had been providing comments for <b>the past four months</b>, both in writing and verbally.

In short: <b>2015; adopted by ILPA; working group set up in early 2021; comments had been given over the past four months.</b></CONTENT>
[role=assistant] <SUMMARY>
## Markdown Briefing

### Key dates and adoption
- **First version launched:** **2015**
- **Adopted by:** **ILPA (Institutional Limited Partners Association)** as part of the **ILPA DDQ**
- **Working group established:** **Early 2021**
- **Comment period:** **The past four months**, with input from **LPs and GPs** both in writing and verbally

### Concise answer
**The questionnaire was first launched in 2015, adopted by ILPA as part of the ILPA DDQ, updated by a working group set up in early 2021, and had received LP and GP comments over the previous four months.**
</SUMMARY>
