[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The evidence includes the INREV DDQ 2022 for Funds of Funds / Multi Manager and explicitly lists the questions under section 3.3 “IT, Cyber and Physical Security.” Below is a direct synthesis of those section 3.3 questions only.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>Section 3.3 questions</NAME>
<CONTENT>Under section 3.3 “IT, Cyber and Physical Security” of the INREV DDQ 2022 for Funds of Funds and Multi Manager, the questionnaire asks the following:

1. Describe the position, responsibilities, and members of the IT function in the organisation. Also provide an overview of outsourced IT activities and explain how outsourced vendors are monitored/controlled.

2. Are you compliant with International Organization for Standardization (ISO) 27001 or any other cyber security or information security certifications?

3. Is IT and physical security a standing item on your board (or equivalent) agenda?

4. Have you developed a formal, documented Cyber Incident Response Plan that describes workflow in the event of a cyber incident?

5. Have you experienced any material internal or external information/cyber security incident in the past three years?

6. Are all servers, workstations and remote devices connecting to corporate networks required to have approved antivirus software installed?

7. How frequently do you carry out IT security training for staff?

8. Do you carry out phishing or similar social engineering tests on your staff?

9. How frequently are full (physical and system) vulnerability assessments carried out?

10. How frequently are internal and external penetration tests carried out?

11. Are there any critical or high-risk points from any penetration tests or vulnerability assessments that are currently outstanding and have been so for over six months?

12. Have you engaged with an external cyber security specialist as a first point of contact in the event of an incident?

13. How is physical access to the server/communication room controlled?

14. Do you have a policy regarding physical access around non-standard office hours? For example, are permanent members of staff on the premises when third-party suppliers or service providers are working?</CONTENT>
