<CONTENT>The TMRS document in evidence is a February 3, 2022 Request for Proposal for “Non-Discretionary General Investment Consulting Services.” It describes TMRS, the consultant’s expected scope of work, and the proposal requirements.

The most relevant section is Section VIII, “Fee Proposal,” which instructs respondents to “Provide the total all-inclusive annual fee for providing all services described in the Scope of Services,” and to separately identify any per-report fees for occasional additional services such as asset/liability studies and a Practice & Performance report. However, this section is only a request for proposed pricing from bidders.

Nowhere in the provided TMRS RFP text is the compensation of the incumbent general investment consultant disclosed. The agreement appendix also leaves the annual fee blank, showing only a placeholder for “Consultant’s annual Fee.”

Based on the provided evidence alone, the annual fee TMRS currently pays its incumbent general investment consultant cannot be determined.</CONTENT>
