[role=assistant] <DESCRIPTION>The May 2020 RFP for the City of Creve Coeur Employee Pension Plan explicitly lists the consultant’s “Core functions.” These functions focus on investment policy support, asset allocation planning and monitoring, investment research and recommendations, regular board communication, performance reporting, liquidity/funding coordination, and coordination with managers and custodians.</DESCRIPTION>
<NAME>Creve Coeur Core Functions</NAME>
<CONTENT>In the May 2020 RFP, the City of Creve Coeur Employee Pension Plan expects its pension fund consultant to perform these core functions:

- Help develop and maintain the Investment Policy Statement.
- Plan the fund’s asset allocation annually and monitor it regularly to keep the plan on track.
- Recommend modifications when there are significant market changes and alert the Board to any concerns or needed changes.
- Provide research and investment recommendations for each asset class.
- Closely monitor recommended investments and meet with the Pension Board quarterly in person, with additional monthly or as-needed phone contact.
- Provide monthly portfolio performance reports and statements.
- Work with City staff to guide fund sourcing, opening new accounts, and tracking investment liquidity for pension payments.
- Work with investment managers, funds, and custodians to ensure timely year-end financial reporting and quarterly updates.

In short, the consultant is expected to serve as the Board’s ongoing investment advisor by setting and maintaining policy, advising on allocation and manager/investment selection, monitoring results and risks, reporting performance, supporting pension payment liquidity needs, and coordinating with external managers and custodians.</CONTENT>
